notes               = "Untitled in source. Rhymed (دیوار است / کار است، ابریشم / نم نم / باشم / شبنم). Walls are the recurring furniture of the war poems; here the wish is simply not to know where any of them are. 22 Shahrivar = 12 September 1996. Imported as a draft with machine / lantern layers; ===translation=== left for Ben. Photo check 2026-07-31 (p171): the page prints تر از with a space — 'drunk and wet from the drizzle', not تراز 'level'. Transcription corrected and the lantern re-read accordingly (it had been forced into 'level with the drizzle' by the joined form)."
draft               = true

===persian===

دوست دارم با تو باشم...
بی‌خبر از هرچه دیوار است...
هیچ‌کس از ما نپرسد...
کِی... کُجا... دیوار در کار است...
گاه پنهان از نگاهِ ماه...
غرق در بوی گیاهی تلخ...
در پناهی... بافته از پشم و ابریشم...
گاه با هم در خَمِ یک راه...
مست و تر از بارشِ نم نم...
من همیشه تشنه باشم...
تو گیاهی خیس در شبنم...
۱۳۷۵/۶/۲۲

===machine===

I want to be with you...
knowing nothing of whatever wall there is...
Let nobody ask us...
when... where... a wall is at work...
Sometimes hidden from the moon's gaze...
steeped in the smell of a bitter herb...
in a shelter... woven of wool and silk...
Sometimes together in the bend of one road...
drunk and level with the drizzling rain...
Let me be always thirsty...
and you a plant wet with dew...
1375/6/22

===lantern===

I want to be with you
knowing nothing of whatever wall there is.
Let nobody ask us
when, or where, a wall is at work.
Sometimes hidden from the moon's looking,
steeped in the smell of a bitter herb,
in a shelter woven of wool and silk;
sometimes together in the bend of one road,
drunk and wet from the drizzle.
Let me be always thirsty,
and you a plant wet with dew...

1375/6/22

